{{also|Dervish}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|darwaysh|darwesh|dervise||archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|tr|derviş}}, from {{der|en|ota|درویش}}, from {{der|en|fa|درویش|tr=darviš}}, from {{der|en|pal|dlgwš|tr=driyōš|t=poor, needy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdɜːvɪʃ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A member of the [[Dervish]] fraternity of [[Sufism]], known for [[spin]]ning.
# {{lb|en|historical}} A citizen or inhabitant of [[Darawiish]] (''[[circa]]'' 1895–1920  {{C.E.}}), the Dhulbahante anti-colonial polity geographically corresponding with Khaatumo.
# {{lb|en|historical}} One of the [[fanatical]] [[followers]] of the [[Mahdi]], in the [[Sudan]], in the 1880s.

